WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.583
There is another form called simple case Simple case
is useful when

00:00:05.608 --> 00:00:10.777
we are comparing one expression against several
exact values Here we start

00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:16.370
with payment status If the status is Paid return
Closed If

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:21.190
it is No Charge also return Closed If it is Open
return

00:00:21.216 --> 00:00:27.105
Follow up If it is Pending Review return Investigate
Otherwise

00:00:27.298 --> 00:00:32.502
return Status missing Run the query in the browser
and compare the

00:00:32.515 --> 00:00:37.576
payment status with the action column You can also
copy the query

00:00:37.602 --> 00:00:42.501
into pgAdmin Compare this syntax with the searched
case from the previous

00:00:42.526 --> 00:00:46.843
slide Use simple case when you are matching one
value against a

00:00:46.869 --> 00:00:51.263
list of exact options Use searched case when each
branch needs its

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:52.346
own full condition
